From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:09:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/29] pipeline: simple: Report the sensor area the software
 ISP output shows

With the software ISP, the simple pipeline handler reports the whole
analogue crop as the ScalerCrop, but the output can show less of it: the
CPU debayer crops the centre of the input when the output is smaller,
and the GPU debayer crops the scaled input when the aspect ratios
differ. An application mapping a point of the image to sensor
coordinates, for instance to set AfWindows, then gets it wrong.

Let the debayers record the area of the input frame they show, map it to
the sensor pixel array in SoftwareIsp::configure(), and report that as
the ScalerCrop. Configure the debayer before the IPA so that the IPA can
use it too.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 .../internal/software_isp/software_isp.h      |  6 ++++-
 src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp      |  8 +++++-
